# Writer 12 (session 7c, F-1). L §3.1 `key K`: "a key of index K, or a thing of kind K (§5.7)", and a movement is a
# thing of its event kind (§5.7), so `x in K` tests the movement's kind. kb[k06]'s attribute `lot: key lots_in` names
# kb[k04], an observed row of kind lots_in (both stated below): `o.lot in lots_in` is true and `o.lot in
# lot_transfers` false, as for the row named in an ask (q4: kb[k04] in lots_in is true, kb[k06] is no lots_in row),
# and the same through a def keyed by the movement (is_lot) and a def whose value is the attribute (lot_of, of type
# `key lots_in`). The attribute's field reads the movement it names (o.lot.day, its row's on). refcore had given false
# for every kind test on the attribute (a movement value with no record, mreads.m_mv_kind_in), q1 and q2 below.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2024-06-30
  start 2023-01-01
  end 2024-12-31

source s "test"
kind funds: unit
kind lots_in: event certain
  leg units: funds
kind lot_transfers: event certain
  leg units: funds
  attr lot: key lots_in
place kop: holdings glb lives 2023-01-01..
place rza: holdings glb lives 2023-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2000-01-01..
input kb: observed
def lot_of[o in lot_transfers]: key lots_in = o.lot
def is_lot[m in events]: bool = m in lots_in

ask q1: (o.lot in lots_in), (o.lot in lot_transfers), o.lot.day for o in lot_transfers over 2024-02-12..2024-02-12
ask q2: is_lot[o.lot], (lot_of[o] in lots_in), is_lot[lot_of[o]] for o in lot_transfers over 2024-02-12..2024-02-12
ask q4: (kb[k04] in lots_in), is_lot[kb[k06]]

version cast
  cite s
  known 2023-01-01
  funds + [glb] lives 2018-01-01..

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2023-01..2024-12
  known 2023-01-01
  covers kop, rza
  opening[kop] = 0 at 2023-01-01 start
  opening[rza] = 0 at 2023-01-01 start
  kb[k03] = (on: 2023-09-12, kind: lots_in, leg units from world to kop amount 90 glb) "l3"
  kb[k04] = (on: 2023-09-12, kind: lots_in, leg units from world to kop amount 60 glb) "l4"
  kb[k06] = (on: 2024-02-12, kind: lot_transfers, leg units from kop to rza amount 60 glb, lot: kb[k04]) "l6"
=== expect
q1 (o = kb[k06]): (true, false, 2023-09-12)
...
q2 (o = kb[k06]): (true, true, true)
...
q4: (true, false)
...
